          `--==[ A N S I / A S C I I - O R D E R - D O O R ]==--'










    - -- 1. Short Description ]----.
- -- --- --------------------------'

    Program: ANSi/ASCii-Order-Door v1.1
   Function: Lets users order an ASCII/ANSI from talented artists
    Authors: Dreamer/Supplex/1oo% - Coding/Design
             Neurodancer/Abyss/1oo% - ASCII/ANSI-Logo
Releasedate: Sun 23-Jul-1995 16:00



    - -- 2. Disclaimer ]----.
- -- --- -------------------'

Use  it,  if  you like, but don't blame me for any disasters this cute prog
does.   You  may  change it for your own needs, as long as you don't change
the credits and don't spread any changed version.

Suggestions are ALWAYS welcome !



    - -- 3. Introduction ]----.
- -- --- ---------------------'

You surely have seen ASCII or ANSI grafix before.  They're the spice on any
good BBS!  So, if you have some talented ASCII or ANSI artists on your BBS,
the  normal way would be:  one mail one of those dudes, and he replies with
some  sort  of logo (or not).  As its often a problem to get the point WHAT
the  requester  of  a  logo  really  wants, we provide you with a solution.
You've surely seen those order doors like "new order" or so for amiex etc.,
so  here's one for CNet/3 now!  We went a bit further than the normal ASCII
order  doors,  knowing that there are dudes who make excellent IBM font gfx
in  16  colors.   So, this door is aware of Topaz/IBM font and 2/8/16 color
requests!



    - -- 4.1. Installation ]----.
- -- --- -----------------------'

This  is the easiest part.  Just include it in your PFiles the way you used
to, or add this line to your BBSmenu below "3; Main prompt" as last entry:

	ORDer	| #0pfiles:1oo/Order/Order.rexx}|



    - -- 4.2. Configuration: ]----.
- -- --- -------------------------'

Load  "Order.cfg"  in  your  favorite  Editor.   The  configfile  is nearly
self-explantory, so just a short section out of it:

---------8<-------------------------------------------------------------

// Config File for Order-Door v1.1 by Dreamer/1oo%
//
// // - double Slash indicates comment,
// == - indicates end of list,
//      blank lines are ignored
//
// You may list a maximum of 9 artists here.
//
// Make sure that everything IS correct! There are NO Error-Detection-
// Routines inside the program checking this Config-File.
// I assume You know what You are doing!

// ************************** NEW ARTIST *******************************

// Artist Name? (max. 23 chars)
Dreamer/SX/1oo%

// Which Account Number in Your BBS?
1

// Comment (max.27 chars)
quite good, but laaaazy =)

// How much Cols are he using [8, 16, ALL, NONE] ?
8

// Does he do IBM- or AMIGA-Topaz-Style ANSIs [IBM, TOPAZ, BOTH] ?
TOPAZ

==

